  <page_number>119</page_number>
  <running_head>VARIA POEMATA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <signature>H. iij.</signature>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" para="true">In Christi media domo, intimisque</l>
    <l n="2">Sanctorum penetralibus, (quid addam?)</l>
    <l n="3">Fortunis opibusque caterorum</l>
    <l n="4">Partis non sine maximo labore,</l>
    <l n="5">Ordo hic nascitur oppido beatus.</l>
    <l n="6" para="true">Dulces deinde fauos suo venenô</l>
    <l n="7">Veram Euangelij &amp; salubriorem</l>
    <l n="8">Doctrinam inficit, atque in vniuersum</l>
    <l n="9">Christi corpus vt inuehat malorum</l>
    <l n="10">Errorum illuuiem, nocensque virus,</l>
    <l n="11">Velis nititur omnibusq; remis.</l>
    <l n="12" para="true">Tum ne sit similis parum Pyrausta,</l>
    <l n="13">Vndecunque sibi parárit alas, E</l>
    <l n="14">caecis tenebris, meráque nocte,</l>
    <l n="15">Quam ignorantia veritatis infert,</l>
    <l n="16">Non cessat, neque definet profectlo[?],</l>
    <l n="17">Sacrum Euangelij inuolare lumen,</l>
    <l n="18">Donec iudicij igne adustus ille</l>
    <l n="19">Diuini cadat occidatque totus.</l>
    <l n="20" para="true">Hac autem ratione constituta,</l>
    <l n="21">Quid restat, nisi clericos vt istos,</l>
    <l n="22">Qui Papam studio sequuntur omni</l>
    <l n="23">Doctrinae caput Antichristianae,</l>
    <l n="24">Agnoscas merito suo notari.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Quin mentem decet vt piam deinceps</l>
    <l n="26">Papae &amp; Papilionibus precemur.</l>
    <l n="27" para="true">P. S. I. C,</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>The closing line "P. S. I. C," is set in the main text as a sigla line. The reading "profectlo" is uncertain; the printed word may be "profectio". The signature "H. iij." is at the foot right. The faint mirrored text on the right side of the scan is show-through and was left out.</notes>
</page>
